{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_84","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git status --short && git diff --check && git diff --stat && sed -n '1,100p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n?? cores/bench/rtl/forward_operand.sv\n cores/bench/rtl/core.sv           | 41 ++++++++++++++--------\n cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv       | 73 +++++++++++++++++++++++++--------------\n cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv       | 42 +++++++---------------\n cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py | 70 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-\n 4 files changed, 156 insertions(+), 70 deletions(-)\n## Implementation\n\n- Registered a 22-bit mutually exclusive operand enable for each EX source inside EX. Bits 18:0 select an EX/MEM ALU bank, bit 19 selects a jump link, bit 20 selects MEM/WB, and bit 21 selects the held ID/EX value. The enable is computed with the existing producer-priority and effective-write checks and held across data-memory stalls.\n- Added `rtl/forward_operand.sv` to select each operand through grouped masked-OR result banks, with the common ADD, MEM/WB, and held values entering at the final OR level. The existing selected EX/MEM result still feeds MEM/WB.\n- Moved the branch-feedback register from IF to EX. The predictor still applies feedback on the same following edge, while the EX comparison now terminates at a nearby register.\n- Allowed the IF replay cache to record a ready live instruction word while ID is held. This removes the replay lookup from its own cache-write enable path; stores to the same word and redirects still suppress the write.\n- Added directed pipeline tests for competing writers, x0 exclusion, immediate jump-link and multiply dependencies, divide completion, a load-use dependency, redirects, memory stalls, and misaligned jump-link suppression.\n\n## Deviations and concerns\n\n- The enable vector also encodes MEM/WB and ID/EX choices so all three sources participate in one data-selection network. No issue-latency or retirement-path changes were needed.\n- Before the replay-cache write-enable change, Gowin Fmax was 75.476 MHz for option 0 and 66.467 MHz median. After it, the three placements measured 76.481, 80.753, and 80.753 MHz: 80.753 MHz median. This exceeds the previous 75.689 MHz champion Fmax by about 6.7%. The full FPGA fitness check is in progress.\n\n## Local checks\n\n- Verilator lint: pass.\n- Formal: 53 passed, 0 failed (first run with `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench`).\n- Pipeline cocotb tests: pass.\n- Cosim selftest and CoreMark: pass with `NRET=1`, matching `core.yaml`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
