{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_77","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'","aggregated_output":"# Balanced EX operand forwarding\n\nRebuilt `rtl/forward_operand.sv` as eight bounded-size masked-result leaves, four pair merges, and a balanced final reduction. ADD, MULH, MULHSU, MEM/WB, and the held ID/EX value now enter leaves alongside the other EX/MEM banks. Both forwarding ports use the same module. The registered enable vectors, producer priority, ALTOPS substitute mapping, and pipeline hold/flush behavior are unchanged.\n\nAdded a pipeline scenario with immediate SRL, ADD, high-multiply, and load dependencies into branches, including bus holds and redirects.\n\nDeviation: none. The formal ALTOPS configuration uses the existing shared M-operation substitute in one leaf; unused hardware product leaves are zero in that configuration.\n\nConcern: the measured gain did not materialize. Gowin option 0 reached 77.001 MHz, and the three-option median was 81.312 MHz with 213.63 fitness, below the 223.78 reference. The worst path moved to a forwarding-select bit through a multiplier input. I also timed alternative four-, five-, and eight-leaf partitions; their option-0 results were worse, so I restored the original eight-leaf partition described above.\n\nLocal checks: Verilator lint passed; cocotb pipeline suite passed; formal passed 53/53 checks on the first attempt; cosim passed selftest and CoreMark with `NRET=1`. The initial cosim build without `NRET=1` failed because its standalone Makefile path defaults the C++ harness to two RVFI channels, while `core.yaml` declares one.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
