{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"test -f cores/bench/implementation_notes.md && sed -n '1,80p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"# MEM result capture in decode\n\n- Compared decode source tags with the current EX/MEM destination. On an ID/EX capture edge, each matching source takes the MEM stage's complete writeback value (the selected ALU or jump result, or the extended load data). The existing ID stall holds decode through a delayed dmem handshake; trap-suppressed writes and x0 cannot match.\n- Kept the registered one-hot EX/MEM result-bank forwarding for the immediately older producer, which has priority over the captured ID/EX value. Removed the MEM/WB data input and enable from both EX operand networks. The regfile's existing write-first read handles instructions already in MEM/WB. No new issue bubble was added.\n- Kept the existing held MEM/WB payload behavior, although EX forwarding no longer uses it. `forward_unit.sv` is an uninstantiated legacy module and was left in place because the pipeline test's explicit source list includes it.\n- Added a pipeline case for one- and two-instruction ALU, load, and multiply dependencies, competing writers, load handshakes, RVFI source values, and retirement order. Existing pipeline cases cover redirects, divide operand capture, held memory transactions, x0, and traps.\n\n## Local checks\n\n- Verilator lint: pass, no warnings.\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`: 53 passed, 0 failed; no fix attempts.\n- `python3 -m pytest -q cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py`: pass.\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: pass for selftest and CoreMark. A first invocation without `NRET=1` reached a harness build error because the Makefile defaults its C++ harness to NRET=2, while `core.yaml` declares NRET=1.\n- `make timing TARGET=bench`: placement option 0 Fmax 78.981 MHz. The worst reported path is now from a registered EX/MEM forwarding enable to an EX result register; the WB-to-EX path is absent from the reported worst paths.\n\n## Concern\n\nOnly placement option 0 was measured locally, so the orchestrator's median Fmax and fitness may differ.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
