{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_46","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,120p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Registered EX result banks\n\nThe EX/MEM register now captures separate simple arithmetic/logic, shift/comparison, multiplier low and three high halves, iterative divide, and jump-link results with a three-bit selector. `core.sv` selects the registered architectural value once for EX/MEM forwarding and MEM/WB writeback. The memory effective address remains independent. `alu.sv` retains its `out` port and both real RV32M and ALTOPS behavior for direct ALU tests.\n\nTo keep the new raw multiplier bank from inheriting the AUIPC/immediate operand mux delay, EX computes the real products directly from forwarded register operands. ALTOPS continues to use the stand-ins in `alu.sv`. Branch predictor training now uses the already registered EX/MEM branch outcome, removing the EX comparator-to-predictor path; this delays training by one cycle without changing redirect or retirement behavior.\n\nConcern: the extra EX/MEM bank registers increase flop count. Gowin place option 0 reports 1027 registers and 63.208 MHz versus the recorded 55.213 MHz baseline; the full three-placement fitness evaluation is pending. The `make cosim` and `make fpga` targets need `NRET=1` in the environment for this core's single-channel port set because their build script otherwise defaults to 2.\n\nChecks: Verilator lint passed. ALU and pipeline cocotb tests passed, including the new stalled dependency chain. Cosimulation passed for selftest and CoreMark with `NRET=1`. The first formal run passed all 53 checks before the multiplier-input and predictor-training refinements. Formal on the final RTL is running.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
