{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_49", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'tail -4 cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'", "aggregated_output": "{\"id\": \"hyp-20260929-003-r9s2\", \"title\": \"Expand the tagged instruction replay predictor to 64 entries\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The 16-entry PC-indexed replay table raised the current fitness to 179.13 by\\nsupplying previously fetched instructions during random instruction-bus\\nstalls. Its PC[5:2] index can retain only one word at each position in a\\n64-byte span, so hot loops longer than 16 instructions repeatedly evict\\ntheir own words. A prior associative 16-word replay window also improved\\nCoreMark cycles, but its search path reduced Fmax. More indexed capacity is\\nthe clearest remaining predictor-side opportunity to recover stalled fetches.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The 16-entry PC-indexed replay table raised the current fitness to 179.13 by\\nsupplying previously fetched instructions during random instruction-bus\\nstalls. Its PC[5:2] index can retain only one word at each position in a\\n64-byte span, so hot loops longer than 16 instructions repeatedly evict\\ntheir own words. A prior associative 16-word replay window also improved\\nCoreMark cycles, but its search path reduced Fmax. More indexed capacity is\\nthe clearest remaining predictor-side opportunity to recover stalled fetches.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Grow the existing direct-mapped replay table from 16 to 64 entries, indexed\\nby fetch PC[7:2], with an exact PC[31:8] tag and one valid bit per entry.\\nKeep the live imem response as the zero-wait data path and use the indexed\\nreplay word only when imem is stalled and its tag matches. Organize the\\nlarger table as four local 16-entry banks selected by PC[7:6], so each bank\\nretains the existing narrow word lookup instead of introducing an\\nassociative search. Fill only on accepted live fetches; invalidate the\\nmatching bank and entry on a completed store, and block same-word replay\\non that store cycle. Preserve redirect priority, branch prediction and\\ntraining, bus handshake behavior, and ordered RVFI retirement. Capturing\\nmore of CoreMark's recurring instruction footprint should r\n…[14515 of 17587 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:349ef2ff8459db3b]…\ntaining branch comparison, correction, misalignment handling, and EX/MEM PC selection.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Exercise back-to-back taken and not-taken branches, redirect squashes, held older memory operations, and misaligned targets; check ordered RVFI retirement and correct control flow.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 195.43, \"delta_pct\": -1.32, \"vs_baseline\": 1512.46, \"fmax_mhz\": 74.693, \"ipc_coremark\": 3e-06, \"cycles\": 3821957, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5035, \"ff\": 2281, \"seeds\": [74.347, 74.693, 74.693], \"perturbations\": [[0, 74.347, 12], [1, 74.693, 12], [2, 74.693, 12]], \"lutram\": 22, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_if/pc_3_s1\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_if/pc_31_s1\", \"slack_ns\": -8.45, \"arrival_ns\": 18.745, \"logic_cells\": 12, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_if\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 12, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-29T14:26:03.989368Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 10}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
