{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'tail -n 8 cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'", "aggregated_output": "{\"id\": \"hyp-20260929-002-r10s1\", \"title\": \"Isolate rare M results from the immediate forwarding network\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current 198.04 fitness champion is limited by a 40-cell path from an\\nEX/MEM high-multiply result selector through operand forwarding and branch\\nfeedback. The full EX/MEM result mux contains high-multiply and divide\\nbanks even though CoreMark's measured kernels contain no DIV/REM and use\\nlow MUL for its ordinary integer products. Those rare banks lengthen every dependent branch\\npath, including cycles that never execute the corresponding operations.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current 198.04 fitness champion is limited by a 40-cell path from an\\nEX/MEM high-multiply result selector through operand forwarding and branch\\nfeedback. The full EX/MEM result mux contains high-multiply and divide\\nbanks even though CoreMark's measured kernels contain no DIV/REM and use\\nlow MUL for its ordinary integer products. Those rare banks lengthen every dependent branch\\npath, including cycles that never execute the corresponding operations.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Split EX/MEM result selection into an immediate-bypass lane for ordinary\\nALU operations, link values, and low MUL, plus a complete result lane for\\nMEM/WB writeback. Exclude MULH, MULHU, MULHSU, DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU\\nfrom the immediate-bypass lane. Treat a valid high-multiply or divide in\\nID/EX like a load-use producer: if the following instruction reads its\\nnonzero destination, hold fetch and inject one ID/EX bubble. The consumer\\nthen uses the full result from MEM/WB forwarding. Preserve EX/MEM priority,\\nx0 behavior, bus-stall holds, redirects, and the existing divider protocol.\\nThis structurally removes rare M-result selection from the timed\\nEX/MEM-to-EX branch and ALU loops while leaving common MUL dependencies\\nsingle-cycle and architectural retirement unchanged.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 8, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Create separ\n…[32931 of 36003 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:5d046e76dfef2800]…\nact RVFI PC and instruction order.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 170.14, \"delta_pct\": -23.97, \"vs_baseline\": 1303.8, \"fmax_mhz\": 63.871, \"ipc_coremark\": 3e-06, \"cycles\": 3754088, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 6008, \"ff\": 2802, \"seeds\": [58.088, 63.871, 63.871], \"perturbations\": [[0, 58.088, 19], [1, 63.871, 18], [2, 63.871, 18]], \"lutram\": 14, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_if/pc_3_s1\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_if/replay_valid_0_s1\", \"slack_ns\": -12.215, \"arrival_ns\": 22.51, \"logic_cells\": 43, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_if\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 19, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-29T15:40:14.341437Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 12, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-29 hyp-20260929-003-r12s2 (regression, -23.97%): Prefetching the predicted successor on replay hits puts replay-word lookup and branch-target arithmetic on the imem_addr-to-replay-table write-address path, whose Gowin timing loss outweighs the fetch-cycle savings.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
