{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-001-r4s0.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260929-001-r4s0\ntitle: \"Register lookahead EX forwarding decisions\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current 50.274 MHz critical path starts at the EX/MEM destination\n  register, passes through the forwarding comparison and EX operand mux,\n  then the ALU before reaching the EX/MEM register. Earlier one-hot operand\n  muxing regressed because it left the comparison on that same path. The\n  register addresses and producer controls are available a cycle before\n  the corresponding instruction reaches EX.\nhypothesis: |\n  Compute the two EX forwarding choices in ID for the instruction being\n  captured into ID/EX, comparing its source addresses with the current\n  ID/EX producer (next cycle's EX/MEM) and current EX/MEM producer (next\n  cycle's MEM/WB). Register those compact choices beside ID/EX and use\n  them directly in EX, retaining EX/MEM priority and x0 exclusion. Give\n  the choice registers exactly the same reset, flush, load-use bubble,\n  data-memory hold, and divide hold behavior as ID/EX. Preserve the\n  existing MEM/WB data retention across dmem stalls, and verify that\n  redirects and divider bubbles cannot create stale forwarding. This\n  removes the destination-register equality and priority logic from the\n  ALU input timing path without adding a cycle to ordinary instructions.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Register lookahead forwarding choices with ID/EX using the same bubble, hold, and flush precedence.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Feed the existing forwarding comparator with IF/ID sources and current ID/EX and EX/MEM producer metadata, then route ID's registered choices to the existing EX mux.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Check both forwarding sources, dual matches, load-use bubbles, redirects, divider holds, and dmem stalls against retirement and register results.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
