tion-bus stalls,\\nthose lost fetch opportunities later become empty decode cycles. A prior\\ntwo-entry predicted-path queue reduced the measured CoreMark run from\\n4.27 million to 4.06 million cycles, but it was evaluated before the\\ncurrent EX retiming a\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20260929-003-r8s2\", \"title\": \"Dire\n…[6938 of 10010 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:e634c7ac22b414bb]…\nh even\\nthough EX/MEM \n{\"id\": \"hyp-20260929-001-r11s0\", \"title\": \"Register the selected writeback value before EX forwarding\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The 212.16-fitness champion's worst Gowin path starts at the registered\\nMEM/WB mem_to_reg bit, crosses the combinational writeback mux and EX\\noperand forwarding, then ends in a multiplier result register. This path\\nis paid on every clock even though the load-versus-ALU choice is already\\nknown when the preceding MEM/WB register is written. The measured CoreMark\\ninterval benefits directly from a higher Fmax without added issue cycles.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The 212.16-fitness champion's worst Gowin path starts at the registered\\nMEM/WB mem_to_reg bit, crosses the combinational writeback mux and EX\\noperand forwarding, then ends in a multiplier result register. This path\\nis paid on every clock even though the load-versus-ALU choice is already\\nknown when the preceding MEM/WB register is written. The measured CoreMark\\ninterval ben\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
