{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_2", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n \\\"hyp-20260929-002-r5s1|Bank EX functional results|145\\\\.60|12\\\\.68|55\\\\.213\\\" cores/bench . --glob '\"'!cores/bench/LESSONS.md'\"' --glob '\"'!**/.git/**'\"'\"", "aggregated_output": "cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:12:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260929-002-r4s1\", \"title\": \"Separate effective-address pipeline from the general ALU\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current champion's 25.527 ns critical path starts at EX/MEM forwarding\\ncontrol, passes through the EX ALU, and ends at data memory. Loads and stores\\nneed only rs1 plus their immediate, but their address currently passes through\\nthe general 19-operation ALU result selection before reaching EX/MEM. CoreMark\\nhas frequent memory operations, so this path limits every measured cycle.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current champion's 25.527 ns critical path starts at EX/MEM forwarding\\ncontrol, passes through the EX ALU, and ends at data memory. Loads and stores\\nneed only rs1 plus their immediate, but their address currently passes through\\nthe general 19-operation ALU result selection before reaching EX/MEM. CoreMark\\nhas frequent memory operations, so this path limits every measured cycle.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a dedicated 32-bit effective-address adder beside the general ALU in EX.\\nClock its result into a separate, unconditional EX/MEM address register and\\ndrive all data-memory addressing, lane selection, alignment checks, and RVFI\\nmemory fields from that register. Keep the ordinary ALU result pipeline for\\nregister-writing instructions; LOAD uses its memory result and STORE has no\\ndestination, so neither needs the general ALU result as its address. The\\nindependent address register removes the ALU operation mux from the timed\\nforwarding-to-data-memory path without adding a pipeline stage, a dependency\\nbubble, or a memory handshake cycle. Retain the existing forwarding priority,\\nEX/MEM hold and redirect behavior, misalignment traps, divider, and single\\nretirement. Expect a shorter address path and at least a 4.6% fitness gain\\nwith essentially unchanged CoreMark cycle count.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 8, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a dedicated\n…[18020 of 21092 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:29daf025a63873e0]…\nline\": 1149.26, \"fmax_mhz\": 64.695, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4272783, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3105, \"ff\": 933, \"seeds\": [63.517, 64.695, 64.695], \"perturbations\": [[0, 63.517, 14], [1, 64.695, 14], [2, 64.695, 14]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.rd_0_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_1_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -10.744, \"arrival_ns\": 21.038, \"logic_cells\": 17, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_fwd\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 14, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-29T12:07:17.378220Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 5, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-29 hyp-20260929-001-r5s0 (improvement, +17.17%): Registering RV32M multiply variants before MEM and forwarding selection, then registering EX branch-training feedback before updating the IF direction table, cuts both DSP-to-EX/MEM mux delay and the EX-to-predictor feedback path without adding dependent-instruction bubbles.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
