{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_5", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'tail -n 8 cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'", "aggregated_output": "{\"id\": \"hyp-20260929-003-r5s2\", \"title\": \"Buffer predicted-path fetches across pipeline holds\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The existing 32-entry predictor already handles most direct branches, while\\nenlarging its table reduced misses but regressed FPGA timing. Fetch is still\\ncoupled to decode: a ready instruction bus cannot be used while load-use,\\ndata-memory, or divide holds stop the PC. The measured bus is unavailable\\nabout 22% of cycles, so collecting predicted-path instructions during those\\nholds can replace later instruction-stall bubbles. The current worst timing\\npath is through EX forwarding and the ALU, leaving room for a small IF buffer.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The existing 32-entry predictor already handles most direct branches, while\\nenlarging its table reduced misses but regressed FPGA timing. Fetch is still\\ncoupled to decode: a ready instruction bus cannot be used while load-use,\\ndata-memory, or divide holds stop the PC. The measured bus is unavailable\\nabout 22% of cycles, so collecting predicted-path instructions during those\\nholds can replace later instruction-stall bubbles. The current worst timing\\npath is through EX forwarding and the ALU, leaving room for a small IF buffer.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a two-entry speculative fetch FIFO behind the existing branch direction\\npredictor. Give fetch its own request PC and advance it on every accepted\\nimem response when the FIFO has room, even while decode is held by load-use,\\ndmem backpressure, or divide. Each FIFO entry stores the instruction PC,\\ninstruction word, and the prediction bit computed for that fetch; decode\\nconsumes the oldest entry only when ID advances. Support an empty-FIFO\\nfall-through response so zero-wait fetch has no added latency. A