{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_13", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'fitness|fmax_mhz|cycles' cores/bench/experiments cores/bench/core.yaml | tail -20\"", "aggregated_output": "cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:4:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260929-003-r1s2\", \"title\": \"Early direct control-flow prediction with a small branch history table\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The existing IF stage always fetches PC+4 and waits for EX to resolve every\\nbranch and jump. Each taken direct branch or JAL therefore discards a fetch\\nslot. CoreMark repeatedly executes loop branches, and its cycle count is\\nlarge enough that removing those redirect bubbles should improve iterations\\nper cycle without changing the divider-dominated Fmax path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The existing IF stage always fetches PC+4 and waits for EX to resolve every\\nbranch and jump. Each taken direct branch or JAL therefore discards a fetch\\nslot. CoreMark repeatedly executes loop branches, and its cycle count is\\nlarge enough that removing those redirect bubbles should improve iterations\\nper cycle without changing the divider-dominated Fmax path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Predict aligned JAL targets in IF and predict validated conditional branches\\nusing a small PC-indexed table of two-bit saturating counters. Form direct\\ntargets from the current fetched instruction and PC. Carry the predicted\\nnext PC with the instruction into EX; redirect and flush only when the\\nresolved architectural next PC differs. Train the branch table exactly once\\nwhen a valid branch advances from EX: instruction stalls can coexist with\\ntraining, while data stalls delay it until EX advances. Keep JALR on the\\nsequential path because its target needs a register operand.\\nA 32-entry table should capture hot CoreMark loops with modest LUT/FF cost.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 8, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a 32-entry two-bit branch history table, early direct-target generation and PC selection; hold fetch state on backpressure and prioritize EX correction. Predict only validated branches and aligned direct targets.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry each instru\n…[98639 of 101711 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:079a57426bf21867]…\nf the registered product in the EX/MEM forwarding result mux while preserving jump priority and ALTOPS selection.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Cover all four MUL variants with sign-boundary operands and immediate dependent consumers, including forwarding across memory stalls.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 172.07, \"delta_pct\": 1.37, \"vs_baseline\": 1319.72, \"fmax_mhz\": 73.52, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4272783, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 4638, \"ff\": 2198, \"seeds\": [70.826, 73.52, 73.52], \"perturbations\": [[0, 70.826, 16], [1, 73.52, 14], [2, 73.52, 14]], \"lutram\": 0, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.lui_result_12_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.correction_valid_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -9.119, \"arrival_ns\": 19.414, \"logic_cells\": 33, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 16, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-29T13:40:02.839994Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 8}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
