{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_3", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'micro_opt|hyp-20260929-001-r11s0|worst path|Fmax' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | tail -n 35\"", "aggregated_output": "4:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260929-003-r1s2\", \"title\": \"Early direct control-flow prediction with a small branch history table\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The existing IF stage always fetches PC+4 and waits for EX to resolve every\\nbranch and jump. Each taken direct branch or JAL therefore discards a fetch\\nslot. CoreMark repeatedly executes loop branches, and its cycle count is\\nlarge enough that removing those redirect bubbles should improve iterations\\nper cycle without changing the divider-dominated Fmax path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The existing IF stage always fetches PC+4 and waits for EX to resolve every\\nbranch and jump. Each taken direct branch or JAL therefore discards a fetch\\nslot. CoreMark repeatedly executes loop branches, and its cycle count is\\nlarge enough that removing those redirect bubbles should improve iterations\\nper cycle without changing the divider-dominated Fmax path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Predict aligned JAL targets in IF and predict validated conditional branches\\nusing a small PC-indexed table of two-bit saturating counters. Form direct\\ntargets from the current fetched instruction and PC. Carry the predicted\\nnext PC with the instruction into EX; redirect and flush only when the\\nresolved architectural next PC differs. Train the branch table exactly once\\nwhen a valid branch advances from EX: instruction stalls can coexist with\\ntraining, while data stalls delay it until EX advances. Keep JALR on the\\nsequential path because its target needs a register operand.\\nA 32-entry table should capture hot CoreMark loops with modest LUT/FF cost.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 8, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a 32-entry two-bit branch history table, early direct-target generation and PC selection; hold fetch state on backpressure and prioritize EX correction. Predict only validated branches and aligned direct targets.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry each instruction's predicted next PC through \n…[170060 of 173132 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:075f424e47b82501]…\nore invalidation, and read/write collisions safely.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Check sequential lookahead hits, taken branches and redirects, held PCs, same-index aliases, read/write collisions, and stores to cached code with RVFI instruction and PC order.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 219.85, \"delta_pct\": -1.76, \"vs_baseline\": 1713.94, \"fmax_mhz\": 78.118, \"ipc_coremark\": 3e-06, \"cycles\": 3553233, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 6298, \"ff\": 2548, \"seeds\": [70.606, 78.118, 78.118], \"perturbations\": [[0, 70.606, 11], [1, 78.118, 12], [2, 78.118, 12]], \"lutram\": 22, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/fwd_rs2_enable_q_10_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.sltu_result_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -9.163, \"arrival_ns\": 19.457, \"logic_cells\": 11, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_fwd_rs2\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 11, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-29T16:28:20.720863Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 13}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
