{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor s in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(s)\n if d.get('id') in ('hyp-20260929-001-r12s0','hyp-20260929-002-r12s1','hyp-20260929-001-r7s0','hyp-20260929-001-r8s0'):\n  print('\\\\n',d['id'],d['title'])\n  h=d.get('hypothesis');print(h.get('hypothesis') if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n  print(d.get('critical_path'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "\n hyp-20260929-001-r7s0 Predecode the EX/MEM forwarding result selection\nDecode the EX/MEM result-bank choice from ID/EX control before the EX/MEM\nedge and register mutually exclusive selection enables alongside the\nresult banks. Select the registered banks for forwarding with parallel\nmasking and a balanced OR tree, including jump-link, multiply variants,\niterative division, and the formal ALTOPS result. Keep the existing\narchitectural result and PC behavior, and align the selection enables\nwith EX/MEM reset, redirect, data-memory hold, and divide bubbles.\nThis removes the five-bit opcode comparison and priority case mux from\nthe EX/MEM-to-branch-correction timing path without changing issue\ncycles. A shorter dependent-branch path should raise Fmax enough to\nexceed the 4.6% fitness acceptance margin at unchanged CoreMark IPC.\n\n{'from': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.result_sel_16_s0', 'to': 'cpu/fwd_rs1_sel_q_1_s0', 'slack_ns': -9.625, 'arrival_ns': 19.92, 'logic_cells': 12, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu']}\n\n hyp-20260929-001-r8s0 Share one signedness-configurable RV32M multiplier\nReplace the signed-signed, unsigned-unsigned, and signed-unsigned EX\nmultipliers with one signed 33-by-33 multiplier. Extend each 32-bit input\nby either its sign bit or zero according to the decoded multiply variant:\nboth signed for MULH, only rs1 signed for MULHSU, and both unsigned for\nMULHU and MUL. Register the complete product at the EX/MEM boundary, and\nchoose its low or high 32 bits after that boundary for forwarding and\nwriteback. This preserves one-cycle dependent MUL issue while eliminating\nduplicate multiplier structures and product registers. Keep the existing\niterative divider and RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS substitute behavior. Reduced DSP,\nregister, and routing pressure should lift Fmax by more than the 4.6%\nacceptance margin at unchanged CoreMark cycles.\n\n{'from': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.lui_result_12_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.correction_valid_s0', 'slack_ns': -9.119, 'arrival_ns': 19.414, 'logic_cells': 33, 'modules': ['clock_ib\n…[1315 of 4387 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:b1b805035e8f78a2]…\n MEM, combine these registered bits\nlexicographically to obtain the exact signed or unsigned branch result;\ncompare it with the registered prediction and select the registered\nsequential or direct PC. Drive the existing MEM-to-IF correction at the\nsame edge as today, so correctly predicted branches and mispredictions\nadd no cycles. Move conditional-branch target-misalignment trap formation\nand direction-table training to this resolved MEM decision. Keep JAL and\nJALR correction and traps on their existing path. This cuts the timed\nEX/MEM-to-EX branch feedback path from a forwarded 32-bit compare and\ndecision to four small independent compares feeding registers. Preserve\nvalid gating, dmem-stall and redirect priority, RVFI next PC and trap,\nALTOPS behavior, and single-channel in-order retirement.\n\n{'from': 'cpu/u_ex/fwd_rs2_enable_q_2_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.mul_result_10_s3', 'slack_ns': -7.584, 'arrival_ns': 17.878, 'logic_cells': 6, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_fwd_rs2', 'cpu/u_ex']}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
