2026-09-29T16:39:42.648829Z ERROR codex_core::tools::router: error=apply_patch verification failed: Failed to find expected lines in /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6-sol_xhigh-v2-rep1/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260929-001-r14s0-hypgen/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-001-r14s0.yaml:
title: "Share a fast segmented EX comparator across branches and set-less-than"
category: micro_opt
motivation: |
  The 223.78-fitness champion is limited by a forwarded EX/MEM value feeding
  EX branch correction. A recent replay-table variant exposed the same
  forwarded-operand path ending at SLTU. The current EX logic describes
  separate full-width signed and unsigned comparisons for branches, SLT,
  and SLTU, adding comparator logic and fanout after the forwarding network.
  Splitting branch resolution into another stage already lost Fmax because
  the forwarded multiply path became critical; this change keeps the stage
  boundaries and issue rate intact.
hypothesis: |
  Compute equality and unsigned less-than once from the forwarded rs1 and
  rs2 operands using four parallel 8-bit comparisons followed by a balanced
  lexicographic combine. Derive signed less-than from operand sign bits and
  the unsigned result. Decode the branch condition as a small selection of
  equality or less-than with inversion for BNE/BGE/BGEU. Reuse the same
  segmented comparison structure for SLT and SLTU, with the ALU immediate
  operand selected separately when those instructions need it. Keep branch
  training, correction, trap checks, forwarding enables, multiply banks,
  divider, and all pipeline handshakes unchanged. The shorter comparison
  tail and reduced replicated logic should raise Gowin Fmax without changing
  CoreMark cycles; verify the new worst path, since forwarded multiplication
  is the next likely timing limit.
expected_impact:
  fitness_delta_pct: 6
  confidence: medium
changes:
  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv
    description: "Factor branch and SLT/SLTU comparisons into shared bytewise equality and unsigned-less slices with a balanced high-to-low combine; derive signed comparison from sign bits and retain all existing branch and trap behavior."
  - file: test/test_pipeline.py
    description: "Exercise BEQ/BNE/BLT/BGE/BGEU and SLT/SLTU on equal, sign-boundary, and differing-byte operands, including forwarding, immediate forms, and stalled pipelines."
