{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git status --short; sed -n '1,120p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-001-r1s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260929-001-r1s0\ntitle: \"Serialize RV32M division to shorten the execute path\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The baseline's 199.8 ns, 156-cell critical path runs through forwarding and\n  the execute ALU. Four combinational 32-bit divide/remainder expressions are\n  present in that ALU; their long arithmetic chains are a likely Fmax limiter.\n  CoreMark should benefit from removing that chain even if each divide takes\n  multiple cycles, because divisions are much less frequent than ordinary ALU\n  operations.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the core's combinational DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU datapaths with one\n  shared 32-step iterative unsigned divider. Capture forwarded operands at\n  launch, convert signed operands and results at the boundary, and implement\n  divide-by-zero and INT_MIN/-1 exactly. Hold the divide instruction in EX and\n  the younger fetch/decode state while it runs; drain older instructions and\n  inject invalid EX/MEM bubbles so no instruction retires twice. Complete the\n  divide only when the older MEM operation can advance, then resume normal\n  single-cycle issue. Keep the standalone combinational ALU behavior for its\n  direct unit tests and the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS substitutes for formal checks,\n  while ensuring synthesis removes the unused combinational divider from core.\n  The shorter timed EX path should raise Fmax enough to outweigh divide stalls.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 35\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add a shared iterative divider, capture forwarded operands once, insert EX/MEM bubbles while busy, and select the completed quotient or remainder.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect divide busy/completion control to pipeline stalls while preserving single retirement and memory handshake behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Give outstanding dmem stalls priority and hold fetch/decode during divide execution without replaying older instructions.\"\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Parameterize away combinational divide/remainder logic in the core instance, preserving the default standalone ALU and formal ALTOPS behavior.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
