hould benefit from removing that chain even if each divide takes\\nmultiple cycles, because divisions are much less frequent than ordinary ALU\\noperations.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the core's combinational DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU datapaths with one\\nshared 32-step iterative unsigned divider. Capture forwarded operands at\\nlaunch, convert signed operands and results at the boundary, and implement\\\n…[19060 of 22132 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:a66a3eb72ca07bea]…\nimprovement\", \"fitness\": 129.22, \"delta_pct\": 9.82, \"vs_baseline\": 966.17, \"fmax_mhz\": 55.213, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4272783, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 2993, \"ff\": 793, \"seeds\": [55.551, 55.213, 55.213], \"perturbations\": [[0, 55.551, 13], [1, 55.213, 13], [2, 55.213, 13]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_5_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -13.002, \"arrival_ns\": 23.296, \"logic_cells\": 13, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 13, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-29T11:35:24.025675Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 4, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-29 hyp-20260929-002-r4s1 (improvement, +9.82%): For CoreMark's frequent loads and stores, a dedicated EX effective-address adder feeding its own EX/MEM register bypasses the general ALU result mux on the forwarding-to-data-memory path without adding memory cycles.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
