{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'mul|MUL|DSP|multiply' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | tail -n 8\"", "aggregated_output": "6:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260929-002-r2s1\", \"title\": \"Retopologize pipeline squashes around narrow valid bits\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current 41.009 MHz champion has a 45-cell worst path reported from the\\nregister file through ID, EX, IF, hazard logic, and back into the ID/EX\\nregister. A redirect or instruction stall makes IF replace the entire\\ninstruction with a NOP, so the execute-stage decision feeds instruction\\ndecode and the load-use hazard network in the same cycle. It also clears\\nthe whole ID/EX bundle. This control topology costs clock frequency on\\nevery CoreMark cycle, while adding no useful work.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current 41.009 MHz champion has a 45-cell worst path reported from the\\nregister file through ID, EX, IF, hazard logic, and back into the ID/EX\\nregister. A redirect or instruction stall makes IF replace the entire\\ninstruction with a NOP, so the execute-stage decision feeds instruction\\ndecode and the load-use hazard network in the same cycle. It also clears\\nthe whole ID/EX bundle. This control topology costs clock frequency on\\nevery CoreMark cycle, while adding no useful work.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Change pipeline squashing to carry raw instruction and data bits freely,\\nand invalidate wrong-path or unavailable instructions with a narrow valid\\nbit. IF should expose io_imemData directly and mark it invalid on redirect\\nor imem stall; ID should capture payload without a redirect-controlled\\nwide reset mux and clear only ID/EX.valid on flush. Qualify every side\\neffect of invalid instructions: EX redirect, EX/MEM forwarding eligibility,\\ndmem requests, dmem-stall detection, and writeback. Mask EX/MEM control\\nwhen its input is invalid. Keep the existing MEM/WB forwarding exception:\\na dmem stall clears retirement valid but retains the previously captured\\nwriter for an EX instruction held by that stall. Preserve redirect,\\nload-use, divide, and bus-stall priorities so invalid instructions cannot\\nretire or alter architectural state. This removes the EX-to-\n…[37778 of 40850 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:cc5b87d46349db7f]…\n trap to MEM/WB control and RVFI next PC, suppressing side effects on traps.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Check predicted and mispredicted branch retirement, branch target alignment traps, redirects overlapping instruction and data stalls, and one-time training under holds.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 171.63, \"delta_pct\": 1.11, \"vs_baseline\": 1316.09, \"fmax_mhz\": 73.332, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4272783, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 4734, \"ff\": 2318, \"seeds\": [70.802, 73.332, 73.332], \"perturbations\": [[0, 70.802, 7], [1, 73.332, 12], [2, 73.332, 12]], \"lutram\": 0, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.forward_select_9_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.mul_result_16_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -9.124, \"arrival_ns\": 19.418, \"logic_cells\": 7, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 7, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-29T13:04:45.969786Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 7}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
