{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-001-r8s0.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260929-001-r8s0\ntitle: \"Share one signedness-configurable RV32M multiplier\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  EX currently forms three separate 64-bit products for MUL, MULH, MULHU,\n  and MULHSU, then clocks four 32-bit product result banks. The FPGA report\n  shows six DSP blocks and 2,262 flip-flops. Those parallel products and\n  their routes crowd the same EX area as the forwarding and branch-correction\n  path that limits the champion to 72.531 MHz. Earlier predecoding of the\n  result mux regressed, so the multiplier itself is the better sharing target.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the signed-signed, unsigned-unsigned, and signed-unsigned EX\n  multipliers with one signed 33-by-33 multiplier. Extend each 32-bit input\n  by either its sign bit or zero according to the decoded multiply variant:\n  both signed for MULH, only rs1 signed for MULHSU, and both unsigned for\n  MULHU and MUL. Register the complete product at the EX/MEM boundary, and\n  choose its low or high 32 bits after that boundary for forwarding and\n  writeback. This preserves one-cycle dependent MUL issue while eliminating\n  duplicate multiplier structures and product registers. Keep the existing\n  iterative divider and RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS substitute behavior. Reduced DSP,\n  register, and routing pressure should lift Fmax by more than the 4.6%\n  acceptance margin at unchanged CoreMark cycles.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Replace four EX/MEM multiply result banks with one registered 64-bit product and retain the operation code needed to select its half.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Conditionally sign-extend multiply operands, use one multiplier, and capture its product with the existing EX/MEM stall, redirect, and divide-bubble rules.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Select the low or high half of the registered product in the EX/MEM forwarding result mux while preserving jump priority and ALTOPS selection.\"\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: \"Cover every MUL variant with sign-boundary and randomized operands, including dependencies that consume the result on the next cycle.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
