{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'MUL|multiply|mul_result|mul.*hazard|dependency|div.*hold' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | tail -n 8\"", "aggregated_output": "24:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260929-002-r8s1\", \"title\": \"Decouple fetch with a four-entry predicted instruction queue\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current pipeline freezes the fetch PC whenever decode waits for a load,\\ndata memory, or division. With independent random instruction-bus stalls,\\nthose lost fetch opportunities later become empty decode cycles. A prior\\ntwo-entry predicted-path queue reduced the measured CoreMark run from\\n4.27 million to 4.06 million cycles, but it was evaluated before the\\ncurrent EX retiming and its Fmax was limited by the old EX path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current pipeline freezes the fetch PC whenever decode waits for a load,\\ndata memory, or division. With independent random instruction-bus stalls,\\nthose lost fetch opportunities later become empty decode cycles. A prior\\ntwo-entry predicted-path queue reduced the measured CoreMark run from\\n4.27 million to 4.06 million cycles, but it was evaluated before the\\ncurrent EX retiming and its Fmax was limited by the old EX path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Put a four-entry elastic instruction queue between the independently\\nadvancing predicted fetch PC and ID. Store the instruction, PC, sequential\\nPC, direct target, and prediction bit together. Fetch advances whenever\\nio_imemReady and a queue slot is available, including cycles when ID is\\nheld by a load-use hazard or data-memory backpressure. ID pops only when\\nit actually captures an instruction. Preserve an empty-queue fall-through\\npath so zero-wait fetch adds no ordinary pipeline cycle. Use a shallow\\nshift-register queue with local push/pop enables and a registered occupancy\\nstate. When full at cycle start, defer a new fetch even if ID pops at the\\nedge; this keeps the decode hold and hazard logic out of the fetch-PC\\nupdate path.\\nA MEM correction discards all queued speculative entries and redirects the\\nfetch PC before another response can be accepted. Keep the existing\\ndirection predictor, EX correction timing, divider protocol, and single\\nretirement beh\n…[34559 of 37631 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:6e9bd92098570deb]…\n payload while retaining memory access and writeback behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Cover all six branch conditions, signed boundary cases, predicted and mispredicted paths, misaligned targets, data-bus stalls, and ordered RVFI retirement.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 198.09, \"delta_pct\": -11.48, \"vs_baseline\": 1534.41, \"fmax_mhz\": 75.398, \"ipc_coremark\": 3e-06, \"cycles\": 3806213, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5597, \"ff\": 2302, \"seeds\": [79.467, 75.398, 75.398], \"perturbations\": [[0, 79.467, 6], [1, 75.398, 15], [2, 75.398, 15]], \"lutram\": 22, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/fwd_rs2_enable_q_2_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.mul_result_10_s3\", \"slack_ns\": -7.584, \"arrival_ns\": 17.878, \"logic_cells\": 6, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_fwd_rs2\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 6, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-29T15:25:34.963384Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 12}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
