{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-002-r13s1.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260929-002-r13s1\ntitle: \"Move operand bypass to decode and remove EX forwarding\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The 223.78-fitness core is limited by a registered EX/MEM result passing\n  through the wide EX forwarding network into branch resolution. Recent\n  attempts to shorten branch logic exposed the same forwarding network on\n  the multiplier and comparison paths. The shared operand selection is the\n  structural bottleneck; changing one consumer leaves another critical path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Move data bypass to the ID/EX capture boundary. Decode the actual rs1 and\n  rs2 usage of the incoming instruction and insert one bubble only when a\n  valid, writing instruction still in ID/EX produces a needed source. On the\n  following cycle, capture the newest EX/MEM result into the consumer's\n  ID/EX operand register, including the completed load value; otherwise\n  capture the write-first register-file output, which already covers MEM/WB.\n  The EX stage then reads registered operands directly for branch comparison,\n  ALU operations, effective addresses, stores, and DSP multiplication, with\n  no EX/MEM or MEM/WB operand selection in front of those units. Keep the\n  existing parallel EX result banks and iterative divider. This should cut\n  the result-register-to-branch and result-register-to-DSP paths that now\n  constrain Fmax. The added bubble applies to adjacent non-load dependencies;\n  the current load-use bubble is already present. Preserve EX/MEM priority,\n  x0 semantics, data-bus hold behavior, redirect squashes, division holds,\n  RVFI source values, ALTOPS arithmetic, and in-order single retirement.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 9\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Replace registered EX forwarding enables with valid-aware RAW detection and a decode-stage bypass from the current MEM result, prioritizing EX/MEM over the register file.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Capture each source operand from the MEM bypass or write-first register file at ID/EX, with existing hold and flush priorities.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Insert a single ID bubble for actual source dependencies on a writing ID/EX instruction, while preserving bus, divider, and redirect priorities.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Feed branch, ALU, address, store, and multiplier datapaths directly from the captured ID/EX operands; retain division's captured operands and all result and trap behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Expose the complete current MEM writeback value for decode bypass, including load extraction and trap suppression.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Cover adjacent ALU, multiply, load, jump, and competing-writer dependencies under instruction and data stalls, redirects, and ordered RVFI retirement.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
