{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('id')=='hyp-20260929-002-r7s1':\n  print(d['hypothesis']['hypothesis']); print(d['critical_path'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"Move conditional branch and JALR resolution to MEM, using the already\nregistered, forwarded rs1/rs2 values and PC candidates in EX/MEM. EX\nregisters operand values and the prediction bit without computing or\nregistering a correction decision. In MEM, compare the registered operands,\nselect the resolved PC, detect misaligned taken targets, and issue a\ncombinational correction to IF and the younger EX/ID stages. Avoid routing\nthat correction through a NOP instruction mux and the decoder: invalidate\nthe younger ID instruction with its existing flush control instead. Keep\ndirect branch and JAL prediction in IF; train the direction table once from\nthe resolved MEM branch, even across bus stalls. Preserve redirect priority,\nwrong-path squashing, JALR link suppression on trap, RVFI pc_wdata/trap,\nsingle retirement, and the existing data-memory handshake. This should\nremove the registered-result-mux-to-branch-comparator feedback path while\nretaining the current correction cycle, raising Fmax without an IPC loss.\n\n{'from': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.div_result_0_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.sra_result_8_s0', 'slack_ns': -8.339, 'arrival_ns': 18.633, 'logic_cells': 15, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
