{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'git status --short; cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-002-r1s1.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260929-002-r1s1\ntitle: \"Move RV32M division off the single-cycle execute path\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The baseline reaches only 5.442 MHz. Its 156-cell worst path runs from a\n  pipeline register through forwarding and the execute ALU to the data-memory\n  interface. The combinational 32-bit DIV/REM operators are a likely source\n  of that depth, and they remain in the timed ALU cone even though CoreMark\n  does not need a quotient every cycle. Removing that cone should improve\n  Fmax enough to outweigh the cycles spent on actual divide instructions.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the combinational signed and unsigned DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU operators\n  with one iterative 32-bit unsigned divide datapath in EX. Convert signed\n  operands to magnitudes at launch, iterate one quotient bit per cycle, and\n  restore the correct quotient or remainder signs on completion. Handle\n  divide-by-zero and INT_MIN/-1 exactly as RV32M specifies. Hold the divide\n  instruction and younger fetch/decode state while the unit is busy, but let\n  older EX/MEM and MEM/WB instructions drain. Insert invalid EX/MEM bubbles\n  during iteration, then issue the completed divide exactly once. Respect\n  existing data-memory backpressure when launching or completing a divide,\n  and qualify branch redirects with actual EX issue. Under\n  RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS, retain the existing one-cycle algebraic substitutes.\n  This changes the pipeline structure while retaining single-channel,\n  in-order retirement and every architectural trap and RVFI requirement.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 30\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Remove real combinational division and remainder hardware from the timed ALU; keep nondivision operations and ALTOPS substitutions intact.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add an iterative RV32M divide unit or instantiate one here, route its completed result through EX/MEM, and emit bubbles while it works.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the divide busy/done handshake into pipeline stall and issue control while allowing older instructions to retire.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Combine divide hold with load-use, instruction stalls, data stalls, and redirects using an explicit priority that prevents duplicate issue.\"\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: \"Adapt DIV/REM checks to the multicycle unit and cover signed, unsigned, zero-divisor, overflow, and consecutive dependent divides.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
