ly and clear its valid bit on a flush, retaining reset and hold precedence without wide redirect-controlled payload muxes.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Gate branch and jump redirects with ID/EX.valid and prevent invalid instructions from creating effective EX/MEM side effects.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Qualify forwarding and memory-op hazard inputs with stage valid bits so invalid decoded instructions cannot affect live work.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Gate memory requests and alignment effects with EX/MEM.valid while preserving RVFI data for valid retirements.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Keep redirect and stall precedence explicit with raw IF instruction fields and valid-aware load-use detection.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Cover taken redirects and imem stalls over wrong-path loads, stores, branches, and jumps, including simultaneous dmem stalls.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
