{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-002-r4s1.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260929-002-r4s1\ntitle: \"Separate effective-address pipeline from the general ALU\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current champion's 25.527 ns critical path starts at EX/MEM forwarding\n  control, passes through the EX ALU, and ends at data memory. Loads and stores\n  need only rs1 plus their immediate, but their address currently passes through\n  the general 19-operation ALU result selection before reaching EX/MEM. CoreMark\n  has frequent memory operations, so this path limits every measured cycle.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a dedicated 32-bit effective-address adder beside the general ALU in EX.\n  Clock its result into a separate, unconditional EX/MEM address register and\n  drive all data-memory addressing, lane selection, alignment checks, and RVFI\n  memory fields from that register. Keep the ordinary ALU result pipeline for\n  register-writing instructions; LOAD uses its memory result and STORE has no\n  destination, so neither needs the general ALU result as its address. The\n  independent address register removes the ALU operation mux from the timed\n  forwarding-to-data-memory path without adding a pipeline stage, a dependency\n  bubble, or a memory handshake cycle. Retain the existing forwarding priority,\n  EX/MEM hold and redirect behavior, misalignment traps, divider, and single\n  retirement. Expect a shorter address path and at least a 4.6% fitness gain\n  with essentially unchanged CoreMark cycle count.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add a dedicated effective-address field to the EX/MEM payload.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compute forwarded rs1 plus immediate in a parallel address adder and register it with the same stall, bubble, and redirect semantics as EX/MEM.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Use the registered effective address for dmem address, alignment, byte lanes, load extraction, and RVFI memory address; leave ALU writeback selection intact.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Check dependent loads and stores, subword lanes, misalignment traps, and memory stalls against RVFI and the reference memory model.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
