{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git status --short cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-003-r10s2.yaml; sed -n '1,100p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-003-r10s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260929-003-r10s2\ntitle: \"Lookahead tagged replay predictor with 32 instruction entries\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The current 16-entry instruction replay predictor recovers hot-loop fetches\n  during random instruction-bus stalls, but direct-mapped conflicts leave\n  many stalls exposed. Expanding it to 64 entries cut measured CoreMark cycles\n  from 3.82M to 3.69M, yet a PC-to-replay-hit-to-hazard-to-forward-select\n  path lowered Fmax enough to lose fitness. A 32-entry table can capture more\n  recurring instructions if its hit lookup is moved off that control path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Expand the exact-tag replay table to 32 direct-mapped words and compute the\n  replay word and tag hit for the *next* fetch PC before the PC register edge.\n  Register that word and hit alongside the PC, then use the registered hit to\n  qualify the current-cycle instruction response when imem is stalled. This\n  removes the current PC-indexed tag comparison from the same-cycle hazard\n  and forwarding-select cone. Cover sequential, predicted direct-target, and\n  MEM-correction PC updates, and retain the registered replay state when PC\n  stalls. A live imem response remains the primary data source. Fill only on\n  accepted live fetches; invalidate a matching completed store and suppress\n  a replay hit on a same-word store in its completion cycle. Keep prediction,\n  redirect, stall, branch-training, and ordered RVFI semantics unchanged.\n  The table-capacity IPC gain plus a shorter fetch-control path should clear\n  the 4.6 percent fitness acceptance margin.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Use a 32-entry tagged replay table and register the selected next-PC replay word and hit on every PC advance or correction; hold them with a stalled PC and preserve fill/store invalidation rules.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Feed the registered replay hit into instruction readiness while retaining completed-store conflict suppression and redirect priority.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Check replay across sequential, taken-branch, and corrected fetches, PC holds, index collisions, and code stores under independent bus stalls; verify exact RVFI retirement.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
