{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-003-r13s2.yaml; rg -n 'hypothesis.schema|validate.*hypothesis' tools | head -n 30\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260929-003-r13s2\ntitle: \"Predict function returns with a small committed return stack\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The current fetch predictor handles direct branches and JAL, but every JALR\n  follows PC+4 and incurs a registered MEM correction. CoreMark makes repeated\n  function calls and returns, so predicting common returns could recover issue\n  cycles without enlarging the replay table. Prior 64/256-word replay schemes\n  saved cycles but lost too much Gowin Fmax on the IF lookup path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a four-entry return-address stack updated only by valid, surviving calls\n  and returns at the existing EX/MEM boundary. Push PC+4 for canonical JAL or\n  JALR calls that write x1; pop for canonical JALR x0, 0(x1) returns. In IF,\n  recognize only that exact return encoding and use a valid stack top as the\n  predicted next PC. Keep the existing direction table, direct targets, and\n  16-word instruction replay path unchanged. Carry the predicted return target\n  with the instruction and compare it with the registered resolved JALR target\n  in MEM; correct fetch and squash younger work only on a mismatch. A stack\n  updated from surviving instructions needs no speculative rollback, and a\n  stale prediction is always corrected by the exact target comparison. Gate\n  updates under data-memory holds and older redirects so calls or returns are\n  never counted twice or from a killed path. This should remove most return\n  correction bubbles with small state and avoid another replay lookup path.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add a four-entry committed return stack, exact canonical-return recognition, and predicted return PC selection; retain the existing direct predictor and replay behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Carry a predicted-return flag and target through IF/ID, ID/EX, and EX/MEM for exact JALR recovery.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch return-prediction metadata with the instruction and preserve it across stalls and flushes.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Register the resolved JALR target and predicted-return metadata without adding a target comparator to the forwarded-operand EX path.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Resolve return prediction in MEM, route correction and target to IF, and qualify committed stack push/pop on surviving call/return instructions.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Check nested calls, multiple call sites, stale return predictions, redirects, memory stalls, alignment faults, and exact RVFI retirement order.\"\ntools/tournament.py:56:# The hypothesis schema's `category` enum, in the order the brief specifies.\ntools/tournament.py:253:        emit_verilog, offlimits_changes, _read_notes, validate_hypothesis,\ntools/tournament.py:297:        hyp = validate_hypothesis(hyp_path)\ntools/orchestrator.py:55:HYP_SCHEMA     = json.loads(Path(\"schemas/hypothesis.schema.json\").read_text())\ntools/orchestrator.py:443:def validate_hypothesis(hyp_path: str) -> dict:\ntools/agents/test_hypothesis.py:275:    assert \"schemas/hypothesis.schema.json\" in prompt\ntools/agents/static_agent.py:100:        \"      No-op placeholder to satisfy the hypothesis schema's\\n\"\ntools/agents/hypothesis.py:340:## Required YAML structure (validates against schemas/hypothesis.schema.json)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
