L therefore discards a fetch\\nslot. CoreMark repeatedly executes loop branches, and its cycle count is\\nlarge enough that removing those redirect bubbles should improve iterations\\nper cycle without changing the divider-dominated Fmax path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Predict aligned JAL targets in IF and predict validated conditional branches\\nusing a small PC\n…[123132 of 126204 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:3ca03c82f7bcfd27]…\naps, and recombine partial products with signed cross terms into the registered RV32M write result.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Drive MEM-resolved branch correction, next PC, and one-time predictor training; route multiply results through MEM/WB forwarding after the interlock.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_operand.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove multiply result banks from immediate EX/MEM operand forwarding without changing ordinary ALU and link bypass.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Interlock a true multiply-use dependency for one cycle while preserving load-use, bus stall, divide, and MEM correction priorities.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Check six branch conditions and misaligned targets, all multiply variants and immediate dependencies, independent followers, stalls, redirects, and ordered retirement.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"cosim_failed: random1.elf [--istall --dstall]\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 14}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
