'cpu/u_if', 'cpu/u_id']} \nHYP: Add one 16-instruction loop stream buffer beside the existing IF direction\npredictor. Record instruction words and PCs only when a ready fetch is\nactually consumed. When a valid taken backward branch resolves in EX,\narm replay only if its complete target-to-branch sequence is present as\ncontiguous, aligned PCs in the recent window. On later predicted passes,\nserve matching PCs from the buffer when io_imemReady is low, letting ID\nadvance instead of inserting an instruction-stall bubble. Continue using\nlive bus data when ready, so first visits have the current zero-wait path.\nFeed the selected word to both ID and the existing \n…[3380 of 6452 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:baa6feadbf191a88]…\nct-tag\ndirect-mapped replay predictor whose data read is synchronous and inferred\ninto Gowin block RAM. At each clock edge, read the line indexed by the PC\nselected for the next cycle: redirect target first, otherwise the held PC\non a stall, otherwise the already computed predicted next PC. Thus the\nregistered replay response is aligned with the architectural fetch PC\nwithout adding a fetch bubble on a predicted path. Use live imem data when\nready and a valid matching replay response only when it is not; fill on\naccepted live responses. Keep tag and validity checks exact, handle same\naddress read/write bypass, and invalidate only a matching cached word on\ncompleted stores, with same-cycle store/fetch conflict suppression.\nPreserve the existing branch prediction, correction priority, bus-stall\nrules, traps, and ordered retirement. The larger table should recover\nsubstantially more of the roughly 0.8 million removable instruction-stall\ncycles while synchronous lookup keeps the table off the long IF data path.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
