{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-003-r15s2.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260929-003-r15s2\ntitle: \"Banked 128-word sequential instruction replay\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The current 16-word replay table leaves many instruction-bus stalls exposed.\n  Earlier 256-word lookahead replay saved roughly 253,000 CoreMark cycles, but\n  its extra memory and routing reduced Gowin Fmax enough to lose fitness. A\n  64-word combinational table saved only about 131,000 cycles and also slowed\n  the PC-to-decode path. The useful direction is more replay coverage while\n  keeping a large table out of the same-cycle fetch and decode path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Preserve the existing 16-word exact-tag replay table as the immediate\n  response. Add a 128-word second-level replay predictor with synchronous\n  reads addressed solely by registered PC plus four, independent of decoded\n  instruction data, branch target, replay hit, and stall logic. Divide it into\n  small independently inferred banks so write decode and read fanout remain\n  local; register the requested full word address with the response. On an\n  instruction-bus stall, use the second-level word only if that registered\n  address equals the current PC and its stored full tag and valid bit match;\n  otherwise keep the existing first-level hit or bus-stall behavior. Live\n  imem data always takes priority. Fill on ready live fetches, invalidate a\n  matching entry on a completed store, suppress same-cycle store/fetch\n  conflicts, and give invalidation priority over fills. A direct branch,\n  redirect, or held PC may discard a lookahead response without changing\n  architectural fetch order. The smaller, banked table should retain enough\n  of the measured 256-word cycle saving to cross the 4.6 percent fitness bar\n  if its resource reduction keeps median Fmax close to the champion.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Keep the 16-word fast replay table and add a banked 128-word synchronous PC-plus-four lookahead table with exact tags, response alignment, live-bus priority, safe fills, and store invalidation.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Check lookahead hits and misses across sequential fetches, branches, redirects, held PCs, aliases, read/write collisions, and stores to cached code using RVFI PC and instruction order.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
