{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-003-r1s2.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260929-003-r1s2\ntitle: \"Early direct control-flow prediction with a small branch history table\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The existing IF stage always fetches PC+4 and waits for EX to resolve every\n  branch and jump. Each taken direct branch or JAL therefore discards a fetch\n  slot. CoreMark repeatedly executes loop branches, and its cycle count is\n  large enough that removing those redirect bubbles should improve iterations\n  per cycle without changing the divider-dominated Fmax path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Predict legal, aligned JAL targets in IF and predict conditional branches\n  using a small PC-indexed table of two-bit saturating counters. Form direct\n  targets from the current fetched instruction and PC. Carry the predicted\n  next PC with the instruction into EX; redirect and flush only when the\n  resolved architectural next PC differs. Train the branch table once when\n  a valid branch leaves EX, even under instruction and data bus stalls. Keep\n  JALR on the sequential path because its target needs a register operand.\n  A 32-entry table should capture hot CoreMark loops with modest LUT/FF cost.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add a 32-entry two-bit branch history table, early direct-target generation and PC selection; hold fetch state on backpressure and prioritize EX correction. Predict only aligned targets.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Carry each instruction's predicted next PC in the ID/EX bundle for later comparison.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch the predicted next PC alongside the decoded instruction, preserving it across stalls and clearing it with bubbles.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compare the resolved next PC with the prediction and request a correction only on mismatch; expose valid branch outcome for one-time predictor training.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect prediction metadata and branch training between IF and EX, qualifying updates and corrections so a held EX instruction cannot retrain repeatedly.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Use EX misprediction rather than every taken control transfer to flush wrong-path fetch/decode state, while retaining load-use and bus-stall handling.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
