ould benefit from removing that chain even if each divide takes\\nmultiple cycles, because divisions are much less frequent than ordinary ALU\\noperations.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the core's combinational DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU datapaths with one\\nshared 32-step iterative unsigned divider. Capture forwarded operands at\\nlaunch, convert signed operands and results at the boundary, and implement\\\n…[13511 of 16583 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:4070fc38a917b57d]…\n, qualifying updates and corrections so a held EX instruction cannot retrain repeatedly.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Use EX misprediction rather than every taken control transfer to flush wrong-path fetch/decode state, while retaining load-use and bus-stall handling.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 12.77, \"delta_pct\": 5.36, \"vs_baseline\": 5.36, \"fmax_mhz\": 5.366, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4203502, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 12672, \"ff\": 555, \"seeds\": [5.204, 5.366, 5.366], \"perturbations\": [[0, 5.204, 146], [1, 5.366, 147], [2, 5.366, 147]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.ctrl.reg_write_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -187.15, \"arrival_ns\": 197.444, \"logic_cells\": 151, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 146, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-29T10:33:47.674765Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 1}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
