priority over fetch prediction and bus stalls. The\n  measured direction predictor should retain its CoreMark cycle benefit while\n  the narrower recovery path should better preserve the current Fmax.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add a 32-entry two-bit direction table, predict validated aligned branches and direct JAL, form targets from the fetched instruction, and prioritize EX correction over speculation and stalls.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add one predicted-taken bit to the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch the prediction bit with each valid instruction and clear it on flush or reset.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Resolve one-bit direction mispredictions without a predicted-PC comparator; provide a qualified branch outcome for one-time counter training and preserve trap and RVFI behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire prediction, correction, and EX-advance-qualified branch training through the existing stages without changing top-level ports.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Flush wrong-path fetch and decode only on EX correction, retaining existing load-use, divide, and bus-stall priorities.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Cover trained taken and not-taken branches, JAL, JALR, misaligned targets, and corrections overlapping instruction/data stalls; check single retirement and RVFI PCs.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
