{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-003-r3s2.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260929-003-r3s2\ntitle: \"Predict function returns with a small committed return stack\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The existing direction table predicts direct branches and JALs, but every\n  JALR still redirects in EX and discards younger work. CoreMark makes many\n  function calls and returns. A small return stack can remove the recurring\n  redirect penalty for canonical JALR returns without extending the current\n  branch-direction lookup or direct-target adder.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a four-entry return-address stack, updated only when a valid call or\n  return advances from EX. Push PC+4 for JAL or JALR writing x1; pop for the\n  canonical return JALR x0,x1,0. In IF, recognize that exact return encoding\n  and, when the stack has an aligned top address, fetch from that address.\n  Carry a return-prediction valid bit and its 32-bit target through ID/EX.\n  For that return alone, compare the resolved JALR target with the captured\n  prediction; redirect to the resolved target on mismatch, or to PC+4 for a\n  misaligned target trap. Keep existing one-bit direct-branch and JAL recovery\n  unchanged. Update the stack once per advancing EX instruction, never for\n  wrong-path or held instructions, so no speculative stack rollback is needed.\n  This should save return flush cycles while keeping the wide target compare\n  off the ordinary branch and ALU paths.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add a four-entry committed return stack, recognize canonical return fetches, and select its aligned top as the predicted fetch target.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Carry a return-prediction valid bit and captured target in IF/ID and ID/EX payloads.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch return prediction metadata with the instruction, preserving it across stalls and clearing it on flush.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Train the return stack on advancing calls and returns and correct only mispredicted JALR returns; retain exact trap and RVFI next-PC behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect EX-qualified call/return training and return prediction metadata between fetch and execute.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Cover nested calls, repeated returns, stale stack targets, branch flushes, memory stalls, and RVFI PC continuity.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
