{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"test -f cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-003-r4s2.yaml && sed -n '1,100p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-003-r4s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"test -f cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-003-r4s2.yaml && sed -n '1,100p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-003-r4s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260929-003-r4s2\ntitle: \"Reduce branch interference with a compact gshare predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The current 32-entry PC-indexed direction table sees about 55,600 misses\n  among 529,600 conditional branches in the measured CoreMark trace. Each\n  miss now incurs a registered MEM-stage recovery, so predictor accuracy is\n  more valuable than it was before that recovery stage was added. The table\n  also maps branches only 128 bytes apart to the same counter, allowing hot\n  branches with opposite behavior to overwrite one another.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the 32-entry direction table with a 128-entry two-bit gshare table.\n  XOR the fetched PC word index with a seven-bit committed branch-outcome\n  history to select a counter, and carry the selected index with the fetched\n  instruction through ID/EX so EX trains the exact counter used for that\n  prediction. Advance history exactly once for each valid conditional branch\n  that leaves EX; suppress both counter and history updates on a held or\n  squashed branch. Keep direct-target generation, the single predicted-taken\n  bit, registered MEM correction, and sequential JALR behavior unchanged.\n  The larger, history-sensitive table should reduce interference and capture\n  recurring CoreMark branch patterns without putting a target array or a\n  wide predicted-PC comparison on the timing-critical EX recovery path.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Use a 128-entry two-bit gshare direction table, hold seven bits of resolved branch history, and train the prediction-time index once per advancing branch.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Carry the seven-bit predictor index from fetch through ID/EX alongside the existing one-bit direction prediction.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch the prediction-time table index with each instruction and preserve it across stalls while clearing it on flush.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Return the saved prediction-time index and qualified branch outcome for training while preserving one-bit correction and misalignment behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect the saved predictor index and qualified training signals between fetch and execute without changing the top-level port set.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Check two aliased branches with opposing outcomes, history updates across backpressure and recovery, and strict RVFI PC and retirement continuity.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
