anch that is not taken, or to the resolved target for an unpredicted taken branch or JALR. Since each direct target is recomputed from the captured instruction and PC, no 32-bit predicted-PC register or equality comparator is needed. Train a branch counter exactly once when its valid EX instruction advances, not while EX is held by data-memory b\nhyp-20260929-003-r3s2 Register predictor recovery before redirecting fetch improvement fitness 117.66 fmax 50.274 cycles 4272783\n  Keep the existing 32-entry two-bit direction predictor and IF direct-target generation. In EX, resolve branch/JAL/JALR outcomes a\n…[3635 of 6707 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:f4732b85b1df66b7]…\nreplay for an in-flight store overlap\nhyp-20260929-003-r7s2 Verify predicted branches from registered operands in MEM regression fitness 171.63 fmax 73.332 cycles 4272783\n  Keep the existing 32-entry two-bit direction predictor and IF direct-target prediction. Pass the predicted-taken bit into EX/MEM with the already registered forwarded rs1/rs2 values and PC candidates. In MEM, compare those registered operands, determine the actual branch outcome, and compare it with the prediction. Drive the IF redirect and younger-stage squashes from this MEM result in the same cycle that the present registered correction redirects fetch. Select the architectural next PC and branch target trap from the same resolved outcome before MEM/WB captures RVFI. Retain EX handling of JALR target formation and its target-alignment trap; unconditional jumps can use the existing correction rule. Train each valid conditional branch once from its MEM outcome, suppressing a duplicate on pipeline holds. This removes the forwarded-operand\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
