{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,140p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-003-r8s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260929-003-r8s2\ntitle: \"Direct-mapped short-loop replay predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The current direction predictor avoids many branch bubbles, but a stalled\n  instruction bus still inserts a bubble on every unavailable fetch. A prior\n  short-loop replay predictor reduced CoreMark from 4.27 million to 3.94\n  million cycles, yet its 16-way recent-instruction search put roughly 40\n  cells on the fetch-to-decode path and lowered Fmax from 72.5 to 61.4 MHz.\n  Replaying repeated loop instructions remains the strongest measured\n  predictor-side IPC opportunity if the lookup is made short enough.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the associative recent-window search with a 16-entry direct-mapped\n  replay table indexed by fetch PC[5:2]. Each entry keeps an exact upper-PC\n  tag, the fetched instruction word, and a valid bit. Fill an entry only when\n  a live imem response is actually accepted. When io_imemReady is low, use a\n  tagged hit as the instruction response and let the existing branch\n  direction/target predictor and decode advance normally; on a miss, retain\n  the present stall behavior. Keep the live imem word as the fast zero-wait\n  path. Do not require an all-instructions-present loop scan or a 16-way\n  comparator before decode. Invalidate the matching entry on a completed\n  data-memory store, and suppress same-cycle replay for a store that could\n  modify the requested instruction word. Preserve redirect priority, exact\n  instruction PC, one-time branch training, RVFI retirement, and all bus\n  handshake rules. The indexed lookup should recover most of the prior\n  replay IPC gain while leaving enough Fmax to clear the 4.6% fitness bar.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add a tagged 16-entry PC-indexed instruction replay table, accept and invalidate entries on real memory handshakes, and select replay only during an instruction-bus stall with a valid tag hit.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect replay availability to instruction-stall control and pass completed store address/write qualification to the fetch predictor; keep registered MEM correction highest priority.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Treat a replay hit as a ready instruction response while preserving load-use, data-memory stall, divide, and redirect priorities.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Check loop replay under instruction stalls, tag collisions, redirect recovery, and same-word code stores against retirement PCs, instructions, and memory effects.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
