{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_4", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n -i 'predict|replay|branch|jalr|return|fetch' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | tail -n 45\"", "aggregated_output": "2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260929-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Serialize RV32M division to shorten the execute path\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline's 199.8 ns, 156-cell critical path runs through forwarding and\\nthe execute ALU. Four combinational 32-bit divide/remainder expressions are\\npresent in that ALU; their long arithmetic chains are a likely Fmax limiter.\\nCoreMark should benefit from removing that chain even if each divide takes\\nmultiple cycles, because divisions are much less frequent than ordinary ALU\\noperations.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The baseline's 199.8 ns, 156-cell critical path runs through forwarding and\\nthe execute ALU. Four combinational 32-bit divide/remainder expressions are\\npresent in that ALU; their long arithmetic chains are a likely Fmax limiter.\\nCoreMark should benefit from removing that chain even if each divide takes\\nmultiple cycles, because divisions are much less frequent than ordinary ALU\\noperations.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the core's combinational DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU datapaths with one\\nshared 32-step iterative unsigned divider. Capture forwarded operands at\\nlaunch, convert signed operands and results at the boundary, and implement\\ndivide-by-zero and INT_MIN/-1 exactly. Hold the divide instruction in EX and\\nthe younger fetch/decode state while it runs; drain older instructions and\\ninject invalid EX/MEM bubbles so no instruction retires twice. Complete the\\ndivide only when the older MEM operation can advance, then resume normal\\nsingle-cycle issue. Keep the standalone combinational ALU behavior for its\\ndirect unit tests and the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS substitutes for formal checks,\\nwhile ensuring synthesis removes the unused combinational divider from core.\\nThe shorter timed EX path should raise Fmax enough to outweigh divide stalls.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 35, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a shared iterative divider, capture forwarded operands once, insert EX/MEM bubbles wh\n…[101818 of 104890 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:6c172a0840871d86]…\n9.13, \"delta_pct\": 5.53, \"vs_baseline\": 1377.97, \"fmax_mhz\": 68.462, \"ipc_coremark\": 3e-06, \"cycles\": 3821957, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5023, \"ff\": 2278, \"seeds\": [65.736, 68.462, 68.462], \"perturbations\": [[0, 65.736, 11], [1, 68.462, 16], [2, 68.462, 16]], \"lutram\": 22, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.correction_valid_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/fwd_rs1_sel_q_1_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -10.212, \"arrival_ns\": 20.507, \"logic_cells\": 14, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_if\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 11, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-29T13:39:22.210647Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 8, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-29 hyp-20260929-003-r8s2 (improvement, +5.53%): A tagged PC[5:2]-indexed replay table recovers hot-loop instructions during imem stalls without the 16-way fetch-to-decode search that cost Fmax, provided entries are filled only on accepted live fetches and invalidated on matching completed stores.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
